    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "This property presents an outstanding opportunity for buyers seeking a renovation project with exceptional potential. \n\nThe dwelling may qualify for the Derelict Property Grant, along with a range of SEAI energy-upgrade grants offering significant support toward refurbishment works. \n\nSet on a generous site and brimming with possibilities, it provides the perfect canvas to create a beautifully tailored home in a tranquil rural location.\n\nThis former licensed premises with spacious residential accommodation is located in the heart of Rylane village, Co. Cork. \n\nRylane is situated midway between Millstreet and Cork City and north of Macroom, in the parish of Aghabullogue Within Rylane there is a National School, Community Park.\n\nIdeally positioned just 40 minutes from Cork City, 15 minutes from Coachford, and 20 minutes from Macroom, the property offers exceptional development potential.\n\nThe property extends to circa. 3,500 sq. ft, the ground floor is arranged as a traditional Irish pub, while the first floor provides generous family accommodation accessed via its own private entrance.\n"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "Notice\nPlease note we have not tested any apparatus, fixtures, fittings, or services. Interested parties must undertake their own investigation into the working order of these items. All measurements are approximate and photographs provided for guidance only."
      },
